# Klave Engine — THE configuration file. Copy to .env and adjust.
# One file for everything: the API and the web read it from the repo root
# (local dev), and `cp .env.example .env.prod` feeds docker-compose.prod.yml
# (production). Real keys live only in your copies; never commit them.

# ============================================================ Local dev ===

# --- Core (defaults shown; uncomment to override) ---
# KLAVE_DATA_DIR=data
# KLAVE_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# KLAVE_MAX_CONCURRENT_JOBS=2
# KLAVE_MAX_QUEUED_JOBS=8

# --- DWG conversion (LibreDWG) ---
# KLAVE_CONVERTER_EXECUTABLE_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/dwg2dxf
# KLAVE_CONVERTER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120

# --- Detection / costing overrides ---
# KLAVE_DETECTOR_CONFIG_PATH=config/detectors.json
# KLAVE_COSTING_CONFIG_PATH=config/costing.json

# --- Workspace accounts (docker compose service: users-db) ---
# make users-db-up
KLAVE_USERS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://klave_users:klave@127.0.0.1:5433/klave_users
KLAVE_WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# --- Web (Next.js reads this from the same file) ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- Registration: open | invite_only ---
# KLAVE_REGISTRATION=open

# --- Google sign-in (optional) ---
# OAuth client type "Web application"; authorized redirect URI:
#   http://localhost:8000/auth/google/callback
# KLAVE_AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# KLAVE_AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=

# --- Lectura asistida por IA (opcional) ---
# Un modelo de visión lee la imagen de cada hoja (cajetín, cuadros, notas,
# marcas) como sugerencia con procedencia. Sin clave, la función se reporta
# como no configurada. Proveedor: anthropic | gemini | auto (auto usa el que
# tenga credenciales, Claude primero); KLAVE_AI_MODEL sobreescribe el modelo
# por defecto del proveedor.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
# KLAVE_AI_PROVIDER=auto
# KLAVE_AI_MODEL=
# Tope mensual de gasto estimado en IA por taller, en USD. 0 = sin tope.
# Es un freno, no un aviso: al llegar, la lectura y el copiloto se pausan y
# lo dicen. El costo se estima con las tarifas declaradas en
# packages/klave_engine/llm/tarifas.py, nunca con un cargo leído del proveedor.
# KLAVE_AI_BUDGET_USD=25

# --- Transactional mail (invitations, recovery, verification) ---
# Leave everything unset and links are written to data/outbox/*.json; the UI
# then tells admins to hand links over by other means. Configure ONE of:
# KLAVE_RESEND_API_KEY=
# KLAVE_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# KLAVE_SMTP_PORT=587
# KLAVE_SMTP_USER=
# KLAVE_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# KLAVE_SMTP_STARTTLS=true
# KLAVE_MAIL_FROM="Klave <no-reply@tu-dominio.mx>"
# KLAVE_MAIL_PROVIDER=auto   # auto | resend | smtp | outbox

# ====================================================== Production only ===
# cp .env.example .env.prod, fill this section, then:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml --env-file .env.prod up -d --build

# KLAVE_DOMAIN=taller.mx            # serves app.taller.mx and api.taller.mx
# KLAVE_ACME_EMAIL=tu@correo.mx     # Let's Encrypt notifications
# KLAVE_USERS_DB_PASSWORD=          # long and random; only inside the compose network
# BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=14

# --- Hosting (set when web and API live on real domains) ---
# KLAVE_WEB_ORIGIN=https://app.taller.mx
# KLAVE_COOKIE_DOMAIN=.taller.mx    # share the session between app. and api.
# KLAVE_COOKIE_SAMESITE=lax         # "none" only when the API is on another site
# KLAVE_EXTRA_ORIGINS=https://staging.taller.mx
